---
title: Chiffon Sponge
source: Baking and Pastry, Cia 9780470055915
yield: 1
---

Line the #cake pans{} with #parchment paper{} circles. Don't grease the pans, as the batter needs to cling to the sides to rise properly.

Sift together the @flour{180%g}, @baking powder{8%g}, and @salt{2.5%g}. Combine with the @sugar{50%g} in the bowl of a mixer.

Combine the @egg yolks{113%g}, @oil{140%g}, @water{85%g}, and @vanilla{4%g}.

Add the yolk mixture slowly to the dry ingredients while mixing with the whip attachment on medium speed. After a paste has formed, scrape down the sides of the bowl. Continue adding the yolk mixture until all is incorporated. Beat for an additional 2 minutes on medium speed.

Whip the @egg whites{113%g} on medium speed with a clean whip attachment until frothy. Gradually add the remaining @sugar{105%g} and the @lemon juice{7.5%g} while continuing to whip, then whip until medium peaks form.

Fold one-third of the beaten egg whites into the yolk mixture to lighten it to a similar consistency as the beaten egg whites. Gently but thoroughly fold in the remaining beaten egg whites.

Fill each pan slightly more than halfway with batter.

Bake at 177C until the cake springs back when touched, ~{20%minutes} to ~{30%minutes}.

> This will probably be closer to 30 minutes, check with skewer.

Cool upside down to prevent collapse, don't take it out of the pan until cool.

> Lemon Chiffon Sponge: Add the grated zest of 2 lemons in step 3 and substitute lemon juice for the water. Follow the remaining method as stated above.

> Lime Chiffon Sponge: Add the grated zest of 3 limes in step 3 and substitute lime juice for the water. Follow the remaining method as stated above.

> Orange Chiffon Sponge: Add the grated zest of 1 orange in step 3 and substitute orange juice for the water. Follow the remaining method as stated above.
